# A terminal with no room for the weather.
#
# The label is `⛆ light rain · 21°`, eighteen cells, and it sits at the right
# end of the rule the logo's pole stands on. Below twenty cells there is no
# rule left to put it on, so the whole label goes and the rule draws plain.
#
# Cutting it instead would leave `⛆ light ra`, which does not read as a
# truncation. It reads as a condition -- a shorter, wronger one -- and this app
# would rather say nothing than say something it does not mean. The same rule
# governs the glyph for an unknown icon code, in `weather-unknown`.
#
# Nineteen cells is not a terminal anyone uses. It is the width at which the
# behaviour happens, which is the only thing a fixture is for.
cache ../cache.db
date 2026-09-11
time 08:00
offset -04:00
size 19 14

enter
